	(text "USB-C INTERFACE DESIGN NOTES (REVISED V2.3)\nProject: OpenMycoNet - BLE_BRIDGE\nStatus: READY FOR MANUFACTURING (JLCPCB 4-Layer Stackup)\nDate: 2026-10-25\nRevision: 2.3\n\nSYSTEM TOPOLOGY\nConnector: J1 (USB-C 16-Pin Receptacle, USB 2.0 Full-Speed Only).\nConfiguration: Upstream Facing Port (UFP) device mode.\nESD Protection Array: U1 (USBLC6-2SC6) protecting data lines against electrostatic discharge.\nData Bus Routing: D+ and D- data lines routed to ESP32-S3 native USB pins via U1 ESD clamp and 27Ω series resistors R3 and R4.\n\n1. POWER & VBUS MANAGEMENT\nBackpower Protection: D2 (SS34 Schottky Diode) prevents back-feeding power into the USB host.\nEMI Filtering: FL1 ferrite bead (BLM18PG121SN1D) provides high-frequency noise filtering on VBUS input.\nInput Decoupling: C1 (100nF) decouples the VBUS power rail.\nPower Net Routing: Filtered VBUS net feeds directly into BQ24075 charger input and provides 10kΩ pull-up reference to EN2 pin (U4) for batteryless USB operation.\n\n2. CC LINE CONFIGURATION\nUpstream Detection: CC1 (Pin A5) and CC2 (Pin B5) pulled to GND via 5.1kΩ resistors R1 and R2.\nPower Delivery: Configures Standard Downstream Port (SDP) 5V detection without requiring active USB-PD negotiation.\n\n3. SURGE & ESD PROTECTION\nVBUS TVS Clamp: D1 (SMBJ5.0A) provides IEC 61000-4-2 Level 4 surge protection on VBUS.\nData Line ESD Array: U1 (USBLC6-2SC6) protects D+ and D- lines against electrostatic discharge transients.\nSeries Impedance Matching: R3 and R4 (27Ω) series resistors provide impedance matching and EMI suppression.\n\n4. COMPLETE INTERFACE MATRIX\nVBUS: 5V power input rail filtered via FL1/D2 and routed directly to BQ24075 charger input and EN2 mode pin.\nUSB_DATA.USB_D+: Native USB D+ connected to MCU via U1 ESD array (Pin 3/4) and R4 (27Ω).\nUSB_DATA.USB_D-: Native USB D- connected to MCU via U1 ESD array (Pin 1/6) and R3 (27Ω).\nCC1/CC2: 5.1kΩ pull-down resistors R1 and R2 for USB-C cable orientation and connection detection."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
